      <activity id="d28ced3d-84e3-5d10-a034-4f843c2e97b8" activityNameId="551569a5-983b-59df-9b66-02f7563b4f4e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, treatment of cables</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, treatment of cables
The multioutput-process "mechanical separation of copper containing cables" delivers the co-products "disposal, treatment of cables” and "copper, from cable treatment, in secondary production, at plant". The allocation is done 100% to the disposal process.;
UUID: 0e44ee17-a5fb-43fa-b2f8-fa8ef8d6323c
This dataset represents the treatment of waste cable from electric and electronic devices. It includes infrastructure, energy consumption, and an estimation of the efforts for transportation. The process has no emissions to air / water.
Location: Data from a European cable recycling company - used as global average data.
Technology: Shredder, followed by a modern grinding machine with current separation technology
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Company information &amp; own estimation 
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0e44ee17-a5fb-43fa-b2f8-fa8ef8d6323c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
